# apps/cms environment. Copy to `.env` (git-ignored) before `pnpm --filter @sam-group/cms dev`.
#
# Same convention as apps/api/.env.example and apps/web/.env.example: this file is tracked, the
# `.env` it is copied to is not, and no real secret ever appears in either. Payload reads
# `process.env` like any Node application — Next loads `.env` from the app directory, and a
# process-scoped environment works equally well.

# --- Database ---------------------------------------------------------------
# sam_cms, and ONLY sam_cms. src/env.ts refuses a connection string naming any other database, so
# a pasted sam_platform URL fails while the Payload config is being built rather than letting
# Payload create its own tables inside the application database (ADR-002).
#
# This duplicates four values from the repository-root .env — POSTGRES_CMS_USER,
# POSTGRES_CMS_PASSWORD, POSTGRES_CMS_DB and POSTGRES_LOCAL_PORT. Nothing expands ${VAR} inside a
# .env file, so keep them in sync by hand; the root file documents the same duplication for
# DATABASE_URL.
#
# The credentials below are the local development defaults from .env.example at the repository
# root. They are not secrets and must not be used anywhere else.
DATABASE_URI=postgresql://sam_cms_user:local-dev-only-change-me@localhost:5432/sam_cms

# --- Payload ----------------------------------------------------------------
# The key Payload signs its own admin sessions and tokens with. It is a REAL SECRET: generate one
# per environment (`openssl rand -base64 32`), never commit it, and never reuse the development
# value anywhere that matters. Changing it invalidates every existing admin session.
#
# Left deliberately empty here so a copied file cannot boot with a known key.
PAYLOAD_SECRET=

# --- Locales ----------------------------------------------------------------
# THERE IS NOTHING TO SET. Payload's locale set is FROZEN IN CODE — `en`/`fa`/`ar`, default `en`,
# `fallback: true` — in src/localization.ts, with compile-time assertions so it cannot drift
# unnoticed.
#
# `CMS_LOCALES` and `CMS_DEFAULT_LOCALE` existed here briefly and were REMOVED: the Phase 1 locale
# set is an already-frozen decision, and a frozen decision an environment variable can override is
# not frozen. One deployment could otherwise have served a locale set the platform does not have.
#
# Adding a locale is deliberately an intentional architecture step, not a configuration edit — a
# change in src/localization.ts, a `Locale` row in sam_platform, a sam_cms schema change (Payload's
# Postgres adapter stores localized values per locale), and translated content.

# --- Demo content bootstrap -------------------------------------------------
# Arms `pnpm --filter @sam-group/cms seed:demo`. Without this set to exactly `true` the script
# aborts before writing anything. It creates ONE explicitly non-authoritative demo page and nothing
# else — no legal text, no contact details, no company claims. Never set this in production.
# SAM_ALLOW_DEMO_CMS_SEED=true
